At SumUp, we are motivated to empower small businesses across the globe. We believe anyone can run a thriving business, and we support them by de-hassling their lives and offering simple and affordable tools to manage payments, finance and customer relationships. Our vision as a global fintech company is to build the first-ever global card acceptance brand, and we are well on our way as small businesses in 30+ countries around the world rely on SumUp to get paid. To get there, we are putting together an awesome team that is committed to one another and to our merchants.
Our boldness, startup mindset, empathy and love for product foster a creative environment for our employees. We value an entrepreneurial spirit and seek to build lasting relationships among our employees. We know that a diverse and inclusive workforce keeps us competitive and provides opportunities for all. We believe that together we can help small businesses grow.
What You'll Do In This Position
Write Infrastructure as Code (such as Ansible and Terraform);
Maintain Docker containers and Kubernetes;
Identify toil and help reduce it;
Automate tasks (Your knowledge in any scripting language, such as Python, Ruby will be a great fit!;
Troubleshoot incidents and problems to find and solve their root cause;
You will be responsible for developing and maintaining continuous integration and delivery pipelines, working on structuring processes in the DevOps area, such as implementing Frameworks, CoE and Development Standards;
You'll be great for this position if you
Experience configuring services in a cloud environment, preferably AWS;
Ruby or Python or Golang or JavaScript or Elixir or Java. Interest in expanding knowledge;
Distributed systems;
Terraform is a plus;
Databases: postgresql (experience required) and mongodb (knowledge required, experience is a plus);
Monitoring tools: Grafana or Datadog or Honeycomb;
Experience with log visualizations;
Advanced english required.
Why you should join SumUp
We’re a truly global team of 3200+ people from 80+ countries, spread across 4 continents.
Stock options plan, Annual bonus plan, Education budget (up to € 2,000 per year), SulAmérica health insurance plan (co-participation), Caju benefit (multiple possibilities: meals, culture, health), Partnership for mental health activities with Zenklub, optional dental assistance, transport voucher or parking space at the office building, meal/food voucher, Gympass, life insurance and more.
You'll have the freedom to work from anywhere in Brazil. Our office is based in the heart of São Paulo, one of LATAM's leading tech hubs and most vibrant cities.
Job Application Tip
We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.

